WEBVTT

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:09.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday the thirtieth of January. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.910
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, got you. Sorry, only just sat down. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous.</v>

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:20.059
<v David Whitfield>You and half the shift, by the sound of it.</v>

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:23.640
<v Tomasz Nowak>Twenty minutes looking at the same van. Lovely start.</v>

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.269
<v Marcus Hale>There is a birthday cake in the office, if that improves things.</v>

00:00:32.359 --> 00:00:37.960
<v Fiona Doyle>There is, yeah. A birthday cake in the office and already a suspiciously large bit missing.</v>

00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:41.429
<v Jamie Brennan>Define large.</v>

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.750
<v Fiona Doyle>Ah. Found the culprit.</v>

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:50.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes an investigation into cake losses—where are we with yesterday?</v>

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.979
<v David Whitfield>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the spinner yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.229
<v Sarah Okafor>All finished, nothing left hanging on that?</v>

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.369
<v David Whitfield>No, all finished. Not carrying it into today.</v>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.349
<v David Whitfield>And tested the newer turbine yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:15.140
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, good. That's the one you had on test when I went past?</v>

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:21.739
<v David Whitfield>That's it. Finished yesterday, behaved itself. Both of those are off my list.</v>

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Useful to have some things actually off the list.</v>

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:37.590
<v Fiona Doyle>Just an observation from me: saw the pressure on the site water dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.159
<v Marcus Hale>Back up without anyone touching anything?</v>

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:47.750
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, exactly. A brief dip, then back. Not putting a job forward for that.</v>

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:58.469
<v Jamie Brennan>Similar sort of thing here—I saw the pressure on the line 2 robot dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Was that still down when you left it, or—</v>

00:02:04.959 --> 00:02:10.560
<v Jamie Brennan>No, sorry, talking over you. Back on its own before I left. Just something I noticed.</v>

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations, not new work we're allocating this morning.</v>

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:23.830
<v Sarah Okafor>And we're still waiting on parts for the Line 3 Screw and Barrel. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.400
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, that's still held on parts.</v>

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.740
<v David Whitfield>So that isn't available to get on with, then.</v>

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.349
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Still blocked, not a job for today. Right, the actual work.</v>

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.830
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team by Wednesday? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:50.199
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Wednesday coming, just so I've got the right week in my head?</v>

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:55.229
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, by Wednesday. Normal priority, no rush job on it.</v>

00:02:57.539 --> 00:03:01.389
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by Wednesday.</v>

00:03:02.039 --> 00:03:04.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Less controversial subject than cake portions, hopefully.</v>

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.099
<v Fiona Doyle>Wouldn't count on it with this lot.</v>

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:17.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Ash, can you replace the seals on the big valve by the gate? Monday for that, and it's fairly important.</v>

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.199
<v Aisha Begum>Monday, yeah? Not something you're wanting squeezed into today?</v>

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Monday, yes. Fairly important, so I do want that one kept in view.</v>

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:34.289
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. I'll replace the seals on the big valve by the gate on Monday.</v>

00:03:35.669 --> 00:03:39.870
<v David Whitfield>That's the seals only we're talking about, not replacing the whole thing?</v>

00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:45.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, just the seals on the big valve by the gate. That's the scope.</v>

00:03:46.639 --> 00:03:51.539
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll schedule downtime for the water ring with production after lunch. That's normal priority.</v>

00:03:52.219 --> 00:03:56.419
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, boss. After lunch is when you're sorting the slot with production?</v>

00:03:57.449 --> 00:04:01.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll do the scheduling with production after lunch. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:07.770
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, nearly jumped in there. We're not saying the water ring actually stops after lunch?</v>

00:04:08.789 --> 00:04:12.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. That's when I'm scheduling it, not an agreed shutdown time.</v>

00:04:12.979 --> 00:04:20.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Ash, the other one for you: can you run a function test on the desiccant unit today, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:04:22.269 --> 00:04:26.120
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, so that one's a fit-it-in today rather than drop everything?</v>

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Whenever you get a chance, but today.</v>

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:38.899
<v Aisha Begum>Fine, I'll run a function test on the desiccant unit today, whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:04:40.629 --> 00:04:44.129
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just the function test, then? Nothing bigger wrapped into that?</v>

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.629
<v Aisha Begum>No, just the function test. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:55.100
<v Marcus Hale>And I'll check the guarding on the main conveyor first thing tomorrow. That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marcus Hale. Tomorrow being Saturday—you do mean tomorrow?</v>

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:08.060
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, first thing tomorrow. I'll check the guarding on the main conveyor then. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:11.839
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, tomorrow rather than Monday. Got it.</v>

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:16.670
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah. My week doesn't end just because yours does.</v>

00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:25.589
<v Sarah Okafor>All right, that's the agreed list. The parts job stays blocked and the two pressure dips were observations only.</v>

00:05:27.689 --> 00:05:29.790
<v Jamie Brennan>And the cake losses remain unproven.</v>

00:05:31.839 --> 00:05:34.290
<v Fiona Doyle>You've got icing on your sleeve, mate.</v>

00:05:35.649 --> 00:05:38.449
<v Tomasz Nowak>Still a better morning than the ring road.</v>

00:05:40.829 --> 00:05:45.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, on that very technical note, thanks everyone. See you out there.</v>
